# AI Architecture

Distilled from a strategy session, 2026-04-13. See `raw/scoracle-ai-architecture.md` for the full notes.

> **Earlier ML plans are superseded.** The backend repo's `TENSORFLOW_ML_PLAN.md` and `ML_IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md` describe a TensorFlow + Transformers stack that's been replaced by the LLM + classical-ML split below. See [Superseded ML plans](#superseded-ml-plans-historical-context) at the bottom for what's still useful from those docs.

## Core principle: right tool per job

LLMs are the wrong tool for structured prediction. The stack is split by problem shape:

| Feature | Tool | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Sentiment / Vibe scores | Role-routed local LLM, fine-tuned target | Language-in, score-out — LLM native |
| Performance prediction | XGBoost / classical ML | Tabular data from Postgres derived metrics |
| Transfer / trade prediction | GNN or hybrid (Neo4j + local LLM) | Graph relationships + performance as features |
| Text-to-SQL chat | SQLCoder 7B/8B (Q4/Q5 GGUF) | Purpose-built fine-tune beats larger general models |

> *An LLM is the wrong tool for performance prediction. That's a tabular data problem. XGBoost or LightGBM on Postgres derived metrics will outperform a fine-tuned LLM at a fraction of the compute.*

## Everything is self-hosted

**No third-party LLM API calls in production.** At Scoracle's ad-revenue scale, per-request API costs (Anthropic, OpenAI) would exceed ad income. Not financially viable.

All inference runs on local hardware via Ollama / llama.cpp. See [[Hardware Roadmap]] for the GPU progression that makes this work.

## Model selection

The priority product direction is the [[Multi-Lens Cognition Panel]]: Scoracle owns stats,
narrative, and transfer lenses over the same sports timeline, then synthesizes them into one
accountable read. Models are interchangeable engines behind those lens contracts.

### Role-routed local generation model

Model identity is configuration, not doctrine. The Rust Cognition Harness routes each task by role
(`StatsLogic`, `EmotionalNews`, `Multilang`, `Sql`) through `COGNITION_ROUTE_*`, with
`OLLAMA_MODEL` as the single-model default. A model swap should be a config change backed by eval,
not a prompt or stage-code rewrite.

Current local generation roles cover sentiment/Vibe, news relevance, narrative grouping, transfer
vetting, Rating prose, and Sigil synthesis. Larger or more specialized open models unlock as
hardware catches up; the durable assets are the data, schemas, prompts, eval sets, and voice.

### SQLCoder 7B/8B

Purpose-built Text-to-SQL fine-tune. Specialist beats generalist at the specific task — more reliable SQL out-of-the-box than a same-size general local model. Fits comfortably on a 1070 Ti.

## Text-to-SQL chat (`ai.scoracle.com`)

Pattern: English → model writes SQL → Postgres runs it → result returned.

```
User query → SQLCoder + schema in system prompt → SQL → Postgres → formatted result
```

Latency on 1070 Ti: ~10–25 tok/s, short SQL = ~2–3s responses. Concurrent users queue — acceptable at launch, revisit with traffic.

## Neo4j extraction pipeline

The local generation model runs async batch over cached articles/tweets, extracting relationship events and writing them to Neo4j. See [[Neo4j Knowledge Graph]] for schema and confidence handling.

```
Text cache → local-model extraction → Neo4j graph →
Transfer model reads Postgres (performance) + Neo4j (relationships)
```

## The unified engine (long-term)

Current path has four layered responsibilities (SQLCoder + role-routed local LLM + XGBoost + Go/Postgres serving). Long-term target is one domain-specific 31B-class fine-tuned model running on stronger hardware, handling all language-shaped tasks — Text-to-SQL, Cypher generation, entity extraction, vibe scoring, transfer reasoning — via a batched local backend such as vLLM.

**The fine-tuning pipeline is largely model-agnostic.** Data formatting, schema context, personality prompting, and eval sets should target the role contract. Swap the engine as better open models ship; the proprietary training data carries forward.

## Implications for ongoing work

- Any proposal to call Anthropic / OpenAI APIs for a production AI feature is a non-starter unless it's explicitly a dev-only prototype. Default to the local stack.
- Personality/voice fine-tuning is a first-class feature, not a nice-to-have. Scoracle's tone (*terse, confident, sports-literate*) gets trained *into* the model, not prompted.
- New AI features should start by asking "what problem shape is this" — language → LLM, tabular → XGBoost, graph → GNN — before picking a tool.

## Superseded ML plans (historical context)

The backend repo contains three older planning docs that have been overtaken by the current direction:

### `TENSORFLOW_ML_PLAN.md` — superseded framework, surviving feature scope

Detailed a four-feature ML stack on **TensorFlow 2.x / Keras with FastAPI serving**: transfer predictor, vibe score, similarity engine, performance predictor. The TF + DistilBERT + LSTM architecture has been replaced by the right-tool-per-job split above.

**What still applies:**
- **The four feature areas are correct** — vibe scoring, transfer prediction, similarity, performance prediction. Just the tooling per feature has changed.
- **Source credibility tier weights** for transfer/vibe signals are still valuable: Tier 1 (official sources, top journalists) = 1.0, Tier 2 (major sports broadcasters) = 0.7, Tier 3 (national newspapers) = 0.4, Tier 4 (aggregators, rumors) = 0.15. Useful as edge weighting for the [[Neo4j Knowledge Graph]].
- **Vibe score 0–100 scale** with crisis/negative/neutral/positive/elite bands is a usable presentation contract regardless of model.
- **Engagement + recency weighting** for sentiment aggregation (newer + more-engaged content weighs more) is a model-agnostic principle.
- **Cold-start strategy** (position averages for entities with no data) still applies.

**What's been replaced:**
- TensorFlow / Keras → local LLM (sentiment, extraction) + XGBoost (performance) + GNN (transfer)
- FastAPI ML router → Go API endpoints (per [[Backend Architecture]])
- HuggingFace Transformers → Ollama / llama.cpp local inference
- TFLite inference → Q4/Q5 GGUF quantization on Ollama
- Hourly transfer predictions / 4-hour vibe refresh → async batch on the extraction pipeline schedule

### `ML_IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md` — superseded status snapshot

Listed four implemented models, a job scheduling system (mention scanner, prediction refresh, vibe calculator), and dependencies on TensorFlow / Transformers / NumPy / Pandas / scikit-learn. **Treat the implementation claims as historical** — the current stack is being rebuilt around local LLM derivation + classical ML, not the TF models described here. The job-scheduling *concept* (async batch on intervals) survives and aligns with the [[Neo4j Knowledge Graph]] extraction pipeline.

### `INTEL_API_PLAN.md` — superseded API surface

Planned three FastAPI endpoints: `/api/v1/intel/twitter`, `/api/v1/intel/news`, `/api/v1/intel/reddit`. Pure aggregation, no NLP. **Replaced by Go-based endpoints** under `/api/v1/news/...` and `/api/v1/twitter/...` (see [[API Contracts]]) and **upgraded** with the LLM-driven extraction pipeline (sentiment / vibe / Neo4j relationships) that the original plan explicitly excluded. The Reddit integration is not currently in scope per CLAUDE.md.

